#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119619 :question/id #uuid "d5a81b39-421e-55c3-90de-d9f4e6489cd5" :question/math-academy-id "e-4795" :question/problem "Determine if $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\},$ where\n$$\n\\mathbf{a_1}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{array} \\right]}, \\qquad\n\t\\mathbf{a_2}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{array} \\right]}, \\qquad\n\t\\mathbf{b}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}8 \\\\ 2 \\\\ - 5\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\}$ if there exist $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} &=8 \\\\ {x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -21\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -21\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+8{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0x_1 + 0x_2 = 3,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $\\mathbf{b}$ does *not* lie in $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119620 :question/id #uuid "94a17888-dcef-58e0-8147-0dec3745f136" :question/math-academy-id "e-4799" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on the plane $\\;\\Pi \\,:\\, \\mathbf{r}=s \\mathbf{b} + t \\mathbf{c}, \\, t,s \\in \\mathbb{R},$ where  $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 1, 4, 5 \\rangle, \\mathbf{c} = \\langle 2, 4, 6 \\rangle$ and  $\\mathbf{u}= \\langle 2, 10, 12 \\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{u} \\in \\Pi$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s+2t &=2 \\\\ 4s+4t &=10 \\\\ 5s+6t &=12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 10 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s+2t &=2 \\\\ -4t &=2 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-4t = 2 \\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad t = -\\dfrac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s+2t & =2 \\\\ s+2\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) & =2 \\\\ s-1 & =2 \\\\ s & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=3, \\, t=-\\dfrac{1}{2},$ we conclude that $\\mathbf{u}$ does indeed lie on the plane $\\Pi.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}=3\\mathbf{b} - \\dfrac{1}{2}\\mathbf{c}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119671 :question/id #uuid "21a6808a-5b1c-5b1d-9bd4-da605fb6d920" :question/math-academy-id "e-6218" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 \\},$ where\n$$\n\\mathbf{a_1}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{array} \\right]}, \\qquad\n\t\\mathbf{a_2}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}- 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{array} \\right]}, \\qquad\n\t\\mathbf{b}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}13 \\\\ - 5 \\\\ k\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\}$ if there exist $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}13 \\\\ -5 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} &=13 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} &=-5 \\\\ 7{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 7 & 2 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 14 & -70 \\\\ 7 & 2 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 14 & -70 \\\\ 0 & 16 & k-91\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{14}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 16 & k-91\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-16{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-11\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0x_1 + 0x_2 = k-11$. Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0 = k-11 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad k=11.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120294 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29ca9bcb-050a-547b-b2da-4f0f41e21511" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312293} {:answer/id #uuid "33e4e32f-db84-5c96-add7-afe0ed9eb2ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312393} {:answer/id #uuid "91785332-a99c-5761-adb1-4c713d6b8094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313134} {:answer/id #uuid "921e2a58-090e-5b48-8da8-da76875590bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313147} {:answer/id #uuid "df4042c6-1a0f-5e6e-b14e-7f66d258577b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91785332-a99c-5761-adb1-4c713d6b8094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313134} :answer-field/id #uuid "af7aa591-d12f-5d0b-8d77-aa97493d51fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314484}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "38bc27cb-fe0f-5096-8126-f66c64c344e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-34060" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=-1 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=-7 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 4 & 1 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 1 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -15 \\\\ 4 & 1 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -15 \\\\ 0 & 5 & k-28\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 5 & k-28\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-3.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-3\\,⇒\\,k=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120303 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0df36293-7642-519e-989b-c1e17518df82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315203} {:answer/id #uuid "237940e7-5e66-5e04-810d-4352d61a17a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315314} {:answer/id #uuid "8d7d7960-d998-5521-90f4-d62f2e5dcd41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315910} {:answer/id #uuid "b6f90b4d-fc27-5736-8b5c-3292c7be6212" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316157} {:answer/id #uuid "dc225773-7e3f-55f2-b9a4-b3e9cdcb7d3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0df36293-7642-519e-989b-c1e17518df82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315203} :answer-field/id #uuid "9edde81d-d00d-5468-9796-d7ae23f5cfcd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316913}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4d12a13d-137e-5159-9c9a-8fb99c09543c" :question/math-academy-id "q-34205" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -11\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -11\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=-1 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} &=-6 \\\\ -7{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2} &=-11\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -3 & -6 \\\\ -7 & -5 & -11\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -10 \\\\ -7 & -5 & -11\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -18\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -18\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-9{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=-1 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=-2 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(-2)=-1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}+(-2){a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 3\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}+(-2)\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -11\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=3\\cdot (-2)=-6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120304 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3e187ae-ec73-5aa1-9abb-af1c37a04e5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117964} {:answer/id #uuid "f599967e-0d55-5000-8d08-18e8b2019415" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117965} {:answer/id #uuid "3f96ba47-3040-5cc5-86c1-c15ce4efec90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117966} {:answer/id #uuid "439eec06-2d3c-58c3-bad8-9890bad26667" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117967} {:answer/id #uuid "63dd41e5-a3ae-56ec-a457-dcd105edbda0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117968}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3e187ae-ec73-5aa1-9abb-af1c37a04e5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117964} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f43defc-60eb-5fef-a664-a3e6a18cbfdc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117963}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "cc1044df-5089-5bf6-ad79-aebf9c199eb8" :question/math-academy-id "q-34207" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc,$ $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,5,8⟩$, $c=⟨-1,-1,-3⟩$, and  $u=⟨-3,5,-7⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s-t=-3 \\\\ 5s-t=5 \\\\ 8s-3t=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 8 & -3 & -7\\end{array}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 20 \\\\ 8 & -3 & -7\\end{array}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-8{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 20 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 17\\end{array}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 17\\end{array}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{array}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=-8,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of $s$ and $t$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc=u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $u$ does *not* lie on the plane $Π.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120306 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3734c4e7-2d56-58b9-ae64-9d84eccc2689" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315439} {:answer/id #uuid "8db74fb0-e83b-5025-b902-46b7c22dbba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315912} {:answer/id #uuid "aac648fc-10fc-5899-80de-3f61d32db10b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316080} {:answer/id #uuid "bf12471c-beac-5673-aa1a-61bae4ae90c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316195} {:answer/id #uuid "ebbf0643-15ef-58aa-bbc9-12b0a9c98f7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316427}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aac648fc-10fc-5899-80de-3f61d32db10b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316080} :answer-field/id #uuid "64b6d89f-f278-5217-96ed-2b3d7bf492cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316785}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3767254e-f5e7-559c-aca3-b6417b0458c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-34211" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨-1,3,5⟩$, $c=⟨1,-5,-7⟩$, and  $u=⟨1,-8,-10⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+t &=1 \\\\ 3s-5t &=-8 \\\\ 5s-7t &=-10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -8 \\\\ 5 & -7 & -10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 5 & -7 & -10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+t &=1 \\\\ -2t &=-5 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-2t=-5\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s+t & =1 \\\\ -s+\\frac{5}{2} & =1 \\\\ -s & =-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ s & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=\\frac{3}{2},\\,t=\\frac{5}{2},$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{3}{2}b+\\frac{5}{2}c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $$\n\\displaystyle s\\cdot t=\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}=\\frac{15}{4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120355 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26d731da-980e-5958-bb11-b7045715cb7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317685} {:answer/id #uuid "4647d462-0bf9-544e-bb3f-c0d7a0beb52d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317792} {:answer/id #uuid "b1531067-2f49-5764-92da-e5ecfde9e825" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318166} {:answer/id #uuid "eaaa3200-ccdc-5f1f-a276-dc2c92322895" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318348} {:answer/id #uuid "f96436b2-dcb3-50c1-b814-2675c7944c08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318394}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4647d462-0bf9-544e-bb3f-c0d7a0beb52d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317792} :answer-field/id #uuid "13796a7d-01bd-5ac0-8a55-2720a5cdf2f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318464}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b46516d2-c8a1-53ed-ad0e-7623ea65bae8" :question/math-academy-id "q-34635" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=-5 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-3 & 1 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 7\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-3 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 12\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=12,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $b$ does *not* lie in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120516 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20f85f4b-26f5-50db-b96c-916dbd611e86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339412} {:answer/id #uuid "9d875afa-7e59-51e5-bea6-2f37d23abfc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340550} {:answer/id #uuid "b6e48be0-7bbe-5447-b9bb-2c25b8e944ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340781} {:answer/id #uuid "bd0306d7-4703-5ffa-a07a-b6e35b29e543" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340816} {:answer/id #uuid "fcbbf23a-a8fc-5115-9c28-cac86f2b465b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341360}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd0306d7-4703-5ffa-a07a-b6e35b29e543" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340816} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac17a9f0-71f7-58cc-b12b-dc681a6d7fcb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341680}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f53bb678-a419-585c-a65e-c61f25afddb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-74560" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ -10 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ -10 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2} &=-12 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2} &=-10 \\\\ -6{x}_{1}+18{x}_{2} &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-3 & 9 & -12 \\\\ -2 & 7 & -10 \\\\ -6 & 18 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 7 & -10 \\\\ -6 & 18 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 18 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+24\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+24.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+24\\,⇒\\,k=-24.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241011 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9af0cd86-ff1e-5239-9722-50f94e89c329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239405} {:answer/id #uuid "a0be7551-7e5c-5636-a7c9-8ef9da132150" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239457} {:answer/id #uuid "a44bd6e6-d3e3-5f61-ba38-c4130f629ed1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239480} {:answer/id #uuid "ae46b645-7b11-5610-bd71-0f1a23d4cc2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239568} {:answer/id #uuid "b95beb87-1375-5d48-a8c9-c7597f30c390" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b95beb87-1375-5d48-a8c9-c7597f30c390" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239667} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecbaf85e-cf9e-5c08-9461-081257f34591" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240744}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a63e4e3d-b5b1-5859-9678-2c18ce011365" :question/math-academy-id "q-105208" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -17\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -17\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=3 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2} &=-17\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -5 & -17\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=3 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=-2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+3(-2)=3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=9.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{a}_{1}+(-2){a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 9\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+(-2)\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -17\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=9\\cdot (-2)=-18.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241017 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28acedc8-6185-5174-a20f-1523f6e81664" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238413} {:answer/id #uuid "911bf0a4-bca6-575a-8b8e-b3222ff2700c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239312} {:answer/id #uuid "aa49ecea-790f-512b-a264-3f8fef658cd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239546} {:answer/id #uuid "deff7940-817f-5ec1-8070-a43c35299f4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240003} {:answer/id #uuid "e11c88b3-593a-53f2-8807-09f826099a04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240031}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "deff7940-817f-5ec1-8070-a43c35299f4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240003} :answer-field/id #uuid "b832e88e-aa6a-556d-b56a-7bd0240d9f74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240651}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4e417e2f-54d8-52fa-a283-38ee2e22e96c" :question/math-academy-id "q-105232" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -7 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -7 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2} &=8 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2} &=-7 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -4 & 8 \\\\ -3 & 7 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 4 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 7 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 4 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+8\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+8.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+8\\,⇒\\,k=-8.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241019 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "351d3eaa-8d71-5eaf-91f1-6a15d982842b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238515} {:answer/id #uuid "521c8347-9356-57c0-82a2-f6f058e2fdd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238763} {:answer/id #uuid "77e423df-6336-5ebd-a988-70ffd97ff91b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239089} {:answer/id #uuid "9e933237-ff23-52d2-a25d-7ee910ab795d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239441} {:answer/id #uuid "b70c1cd0-e286-53f1-ba39-4e8669a377a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239650}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "521c8347-9356-57c0-82a2-f6f058e2fdd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238763} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca08aa7d-69a4-53e7-9a42-33232fc442bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "847914f8-60db-55a2-9155-7cfe231e6bcb" :question/math-academy-id "q-105237" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2} &=3 \\\\ 3{x}_{2} &=-6 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+12{x}_{2} &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6 \\\\ -3 & 12 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+9\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+9\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+9.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+9\\,⇒\\,k=-9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241021 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "285f60c4-cfc6-509d-a8ca-df316a92348e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238408} {:answer/id #uuid "306f3ae9-9703-5c61-9e1f-a029efeb6fbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238477} {:answer/id #uuid "7197f81b-8003-5f00-b98f-69a60e60b685" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239030} {:answer/id #uuid "7aef6609-8c36-5411-ba86-81d4a40f69b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239115} {:answer/id #uuid "db09174f-1cdc-5bdb-8120-63756b097fdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239966}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db09174f-1cdc-5bdb-8120-63756b097fdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239966} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f5dbe15-3666-592c-9f7a-5c21bff9ad15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240504}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "edff4129-bf9d-5206-854e-d3e5b43ca237" :question/math-academy-id "q-105253" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc,$ $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨-1,3,2⟩$, $c=⟨2,-1,-1⟩$, and  $u=⟨5,-5,-4⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+2t &=5 \\\\ 3s-t &=-5 \\\\ 2s-t &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+2t &=5 \\\\ t &=2 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt=2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s+2t & =5 \\\\ -s+2(2) & =5 \\\\ -s+4 & =5 \\\\ s & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=-1,\\,t=2,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=-b+2c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=(-1)\\cdot 2=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241023 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "202fca4b-d4db-559c-86f9-155db3d13c64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238333} {:answer/id #uuid "2b56c1db-87eb-5ec9-914d-30a522b26fe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238442} {:answer/id #uuid "6182bb36-df22-5b55-8de2-18be6f4e6edb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238911} {:answer/id #uuid "a846d2c7-f2b2-52b6-aa5d-db3effda179c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239517} {:answer/id #uuid "f503a4ab-d69a-5e93-a2e0-b67020545fa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240218}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6182bb36-df22-5b55-8de2-18be6f4e6edb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238911} :answer-field/id #uuid "13f36fa9-d65b-5d54-8f7f-9bbf30419197" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240360}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "caedc8c2-ba3c-5e61-ad1f-0d5eafbb8652" :question/math-academy-id "q-105257" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc,$ $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,-2,-1⟩$, $c=⟨-4,5,-1⟩$, and  $u=⟨1,1,4⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s-4t &=1 \\\\ -2s+5t &=1 \\\\ -s-t &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s-4t &=1 \\\\ t &=-1 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt=-1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s-4t & =1 \\\\ s-4(-1) & =1 \\\\ s+4 & =1 \\\\ s & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=-3,\\,t=-1,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=-3b-c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=(-3)\\cdot (-1)=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241024 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d43760f-5307-568e-a84e-682220ff1a4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238868} {:answer/id #uuid "880f352c-1248-5802-aad6-0f18fb03e119" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239238} {:answer/id #uuid "9f0f8258-6bb9-5599-9ae6-72aed7ee6ef6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239444} {:answer/id #uuid "bc37d1db-6d5f-55cb-9d65-e53eb7a7a21a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239696} {:answer/id #uuid "becf26eb-4fe8-5d5a-9c5d-01dc6db2f13e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc37d1db-6d5f-55cb-9d65-e53eb7a7a21a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239696} :answer-field/id #uuid "8da127e5-a769-5b87-898c-b652f5625bd9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240581}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1b477b81-717a-5a90-91d6-e069d7ac13b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-105261" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc,$ $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,-1,3⟩$, $c=⟨-2,4,-3⟩$, and  $u=⟨3,-7,3⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s-2t &=3 \\\\ -s+4t &=-7 \\\\ 3s-3t &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s-2t &=3 \\\\ t &=-2 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt=-2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s-2t & =3 \\\\ s-2(-2) & =3 \\\\ s+4 & =3 \\\\ s & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=-1,\\,t=-2,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=-b-2c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=(-1)\\cdot (-2)=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241025 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "145063fc-8e8e-5c5e-b9c0-4ce50643aeca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238221} {:answer/id #uuid "4fd14ba1-3c05-5721-9490-57e8bf80fea6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238742} {:answer/id #uuid "a01540c4-5818-561d-9151-d28aeb0e7fe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239452} {:answer/id #uuid "b4e4047e-41ea-50d0-ab94-58e7363cb874" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239637} {:answer/id #uuid "ebdd9058-9132-5515-90b7-33b231320d45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240131}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fd14ba1-3c05-5721-9490-57e8bf80fea6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238742} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dee8bc9-1a1f-59f0-8b66-162d23f34c3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240468}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8c4cb4f7-2d57-5ca9-8ffa-a4fe4548b0de" :question/math-academy-id "q-105265" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc,$ $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨-1,-1,4⟩$, $c=⟨-3,-8,14⟩$, and  $u=⟨5,-10,-14⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -14\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s-3t &=5 \\\\ -s-8t &=-10 \\\\ 4s+14t &=-14\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -8 & -10 \\\\ 4 & 14 & -14\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -15 \\\\ 4 & 14 & -14\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -15 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s-3t &=5 \\\\ t &=3 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt=3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s-3t & =5 \\\\ -s-3(3) & =5 \\\\ -s-9 & =5 \\\\ s & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=-14,\\,t=3,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=-14b+3c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=(-14)\\cdot 3=-42.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314972 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "077cc4da-3c12-5749-87e3-9136fa56ff18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312025} {:answer/id #uuid "39d686df-f396-5c82-92b8-3b075c274d61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312445} {:answer/id #uuid "4dd5ec6b-997e-5c4c-82cd-f74e85dcbdf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312607} {:answer/id #uuid "7578cf04-a90c-5b5d-ac09-511fd3e57a8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312909} {:answer/id #uuid "2efb3d59-10d0-57b0-b6f6-06c1b609ee7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422770}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7578cf04-a90c-5b5d-ac09-511fd3e57a8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312909} :answer-field/id #uuid "901fd7a3-f614-5740-8413-9326f82935f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314396}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dffa9b37-7313-5190-ae5f-372cf9f5aaea" :question/math-academy-id "q-34058" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=1 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=1 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 7\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=1 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=1 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=1.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-1=1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=2\\cdot 1=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315058 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4353f2a2-2e1f-5b21-a610-9bc1d73de9eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312513} {:answer/id #uuid "5a50f3ee-4329-5f14-85d9-cd33cdb2bfaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312695} {:answer/id #uuid "95778461-811f-5b4c-bb40-bd404063421e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313170} {:answer/id #uuid "b72923b2-e566-5436-984b-89faeb74608d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313400} {:answer/id #uuid "e264f385-ccd1-57b4-a97a-4878b9b02343" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a50f3ee-4329-5f14-85d9-cd33cdb2bfaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312695} :answer-field/id #uuid "535982b4-ac83-5175-baa7-29e64cb50acc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314243}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d123ca06-d8b5-58e1-a29a-b212c006eac8" :question/math-academy-id "q-34115" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1} &=-2 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=4 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 31\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=31,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $b$ does *not* lie in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315059 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "683c75de-7b34-50d6-88f2-6c51a3c7f829" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312792} {:answer/id #uuid "923048c9-ff86-55c4-bcc3-03777aa67776" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313149} {:answer/id #uuid "afaf5d38-ccd2-55f1-a847-9241b631f84f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313345} {:answer/id #uuid "dd4e5aec-7f80-5329-8295-b30810fc13fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313716} {:answer/id #uuid "e2641fa7-4060-5129-9314-eb56f0e0a24d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313758}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2641fa7-4060-5129-9314-eb56f0e0a24d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313758} :answer-field/id #uuid "4764b730-de51-591f-8dc2-a6719ee618fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "6c8923fc-6353-5c69-b3ea-6ae80c516e61" :question/math-academy-id "q-34117" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, ${a}_{3}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+6{x}_{3} &=-4 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=-9 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 6 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 18 & -21 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-18{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+6{x}_{3} &=-4 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=-3 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+6(-1)=-4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+(-3){a}_{2}+(-1){a}_{3} & =b \\\\ 2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+(-3)\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+(-1)\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=2\\cdot (-3)\\cdot (-1)=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317208 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08ca81bd-a843-517f-a7ef-72a2701907bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315161} {:answer/id #uuid "31e52722-b368-5c85-8ea5-9c73d21f221f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315408} {:answer/id #uuid "3a3a18e5-9318-5ff6-9f5d-5297ea2e47b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315452} {:answer/id #uuid "43670fca-c17e-5839-b7bf-2ab9ba603b7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315509} {:answer/id #uuid "8a0a632c-b0f2-53fa-9828-61b94974deed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43670fca-c17e-5839-b7bf-2ab9ba603b7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315509} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed15606e-311e-585d-8930-70b904dd77b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317109}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "725d2e8b-44d5-5b25-872e-7c29b876b698" :question/math-academy-id "q-34212" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc,$ $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,7,-3⟩$, $c=⟨-8,10,-4⟩$, and  $u=⟨6,9,-4⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s-8t &=6 \\\\ 7s+10t &=9 \\\\ -3s-4t &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 10 & 9 \\\\ -3 & -4 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 66 & -33 \\\\ -3 & -4 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 66 & -33 \\\\ 0 & -28 & 14\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{66}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & -28 & 14\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+28{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s-8t &=6 \\\\ t &=-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s-8t & =6 \\\\ s-8\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) & =6 \\\\ s+4 & =6 \\\\ s & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=2,\\,t=-\\frac{1}{2},$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=2b-\\frac{1}{2}c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=2\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317213 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d12c5f6-3b92-5441-a0fc-3952c1a70749" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315285} {:answer/id #uuid "2be071fa-e50f-5e15-af2e-800d12bec8db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315374} {:answer/id #uuid "40c87c4f-e4ad-5573-b56b-bbf8371657d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315491} {:answer/id #uuid "719e49b9-6453-5c6f-ae8b-fb5f2080b954" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315762} {:answer/id #uuid "385e50bb-f4df-5245-a484-97539f7d5c09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422778}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40c87c4f-e4ad-5573-b56b-bbf8371657d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315491} :answer-field/id #uuid "8429c92b-0897-5b2d-8856-66b5640c1f28" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316855}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "54dedc31-eea3-5db1-a0e4-025cee199163" :question/math-academy-id "q-34218" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, ${a}_{3}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -14\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -14\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{3} &=6 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3} &=-14 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=-14\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -2 & 6 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 6 & -14 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & -14\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & -14\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{3} &=6 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=4 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=-2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-2.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2(-2)=6\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+4{a}_{2}+(-2){a}_{3} & =b \\\\ 2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+4\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+(-2)\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -14\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=2\\cdot 4\\cdot (-2)=-16.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342223 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "120b91cf-0db6-5fff-9cd2-96b7e554a40a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339285} {:answer/id #uuid "14e37e35-842f-5038-9d62-28d1f13c1bd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339313} {:answer/id #uuid "2d7657e7-1a18-56b9-93e9-58660f379564" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339526} {:answer/id #uuid "67d6a9b4-19f3-511b-aa8f-ade40252120a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340051} {:answer/id #uuid "f805952e-7829-54ab-97f1-32e7a06c683e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67d6a9b4-19f3-511b-aa8f-ade40252120a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340051} :answer-field/id #uuid "e16bd03e-9440-52af-87df-1a7859a2c251" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341783}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b39a9eda-2020-5222-b891-a65118115aa0" :question/math-academy-id "q-74546" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=2 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+10{x}_{2} &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 10 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=2 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=-2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+3(-2)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=8.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{a}_{1}+(-2){a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 8\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+(-2)\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=8\\cdot (-2)=-16.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342228 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28049f08-5684-5304-ad3d-9f534b59f279" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339478} {:answer/id #uuid "67519cd7-cc6e-5952-bf35-4a4a24da747e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340043} {:answer/id #uuid "79c14b9a-0376-5405-a220-fdac02f464da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340214} {:answer/id #uuid "92c70a7d-6a91-5cb6-8d17-c5ff99a5580f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340448} {:answer/id #uuid "b383d39f-e410-5314-b906-611aa1b45702" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340760}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67519cd7-cc6e-5952-bf35-4a4a24da747e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340043} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6c41871-59a4-56ef-80fe-7d004904e3a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341700}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "62066547-f160-5da7-be83-cd71028d6d36" :question/math-academy-id "q-74556" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2} &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 6 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 6 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 9 & k-6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-9{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-15\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-15.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-15\\,⇒\\,k=15.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342229 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18733bfc-c516-57fc-8204-98be886fd6cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339347} {:answer/id #uuid "1ee95a79-bba5-59cc-9f71-c0051ce3fca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339398} {:answer/id #uuid "4d1a1e05-cb85-543e-b3c6-80325298b9b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175921860