egin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}5 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 12 \\\\ 2 & -1 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 1 & k+6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{6}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & k+6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+4\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+4.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+4\\,⇒\\,k=-4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342240 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18285e78-b775-52d3-9ce4-8875b58cd9dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339343} {:answer/id #uuid "1be7024d-e144-5979-8991-a6fe697cbc56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339367} {:answer/id #uuid "39886f7e-3d38-5ba7-ae30-319ca5a0cc0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339646} {:answer/id #uuid "7c3953fd-8be9-5eec-b885-1d99ddc7adf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340246} {:answer/id #uuid "bb9dd147-f938-5d4d-8bda-da9705de4409" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340808}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1be7024d-e144-5979-8991-a6fe697cbc56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339367} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8ed9efb-9d03-53c8-9fad-57fa155b57a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341732}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "55c44296-8bfb-53c1-b37c-07eab30d99a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-74598" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨-1,2,3⟩$, $c=⟨3,-7,-9⟩$, and  $u=⟨2,-3,-6⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+3t &=2 \\\\ 2s-7t &=-3 \\\\ 3s-9t &=-6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -7 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -9 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -9 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+3t &=2 \\\\ -t &=1 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-t=1\\,⟹\\,t=-1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s+3t & =2 \\\\ -s+3(-1) & =2 \\\\ -s & =5 \\\\ s & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=-5,\\,t=-1,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=-5b-c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=(-5)\\cdot (-1)=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342241 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2486b2f1-5c38-55cd-a205-21e202e09c4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339446} {:answer/id #uuid "2cadd916-ed59-5b50-9446-268229ac2732" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339516} {:answer/id #uuid "4cc45ccf-adc7-53ad-a852-af95cfc40061" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339825} {:answer/id #uuid "733ba44c-1a53-5f59-af78-2d354dda43f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340150} {:answer/id #uuid "7caedebc-c212-5602-b507-20831a0f0c1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340251}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cadd916-ed59-5b50-9446-268229ac2732" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339516} :answer-field/id #uuid "520ff562-4653-55df-b4dc-8fbcaed97a63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341528}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d6c3f74b-5a27-519e-8d22-1736702759dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-74599" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨-1,4,3⟩$, $c=⟨1,-6,-7⟩$, and  $u=⟨1,-10,-15⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -15\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+t &=1 \\\\ 4s-6t &=-10 \\\\ 3s-7t &=-15\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -6 & -10 \\\\ 3 & -7 & -15\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 3 & -7 & -15\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+t &=1 \\\\ -2t &=-6 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-2t=-6\\,⟹\\,t=3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s+t & =1 \\\\ -s+3 & =1 \\\\ -s & =-2 \\\\ s & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=2,\\,t=3,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=2b+3c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=2\\cdot 3=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342243 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06b3b852-a49c-5eeb-92f6-f26e6d188a47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339184} {:answer/id #uuid "191397de-4f1f-5ce1-a2c1-b8de6e1df5ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339350} {:answer/id #uuid "459245c0-1823-5440-b561-9af08e968b96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339745} {:answer/id #uuid "6e7685b0-ef1b-58de-ad96-cbeee1b70636" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340105} {:answer/id #uuid "9fd09f6d-fcdf-5876-9523-8e01ec65ed87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340574}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e7685b0-ef1b-58de-ad96-cbeee1b70636" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340105} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bebdfbe-9cbd-5971-9a6a-74e16cc92f99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341655}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dcb29558-7233-531f-8a7f-7d0b5b7173b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-74602" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,7,-6⟩$, $c=⟨-2,-10,12⟩$, and  $u=⟨2,11,-12⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 11 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s-2t &=2 \\\\ 7s-10t &=11 \\\\ -6s+12t &=-12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 7 & -10 & 11 \\\\ -6 & 12 & -12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -6 & 12 & -12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s-2t &=2 \\\\ 4t &=-3 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n4t=-3\\,⟹\\,t=-\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s-2t & =2 \\\\ s-2\\left(-\\frac{3}{4}\\right) & =2 \\\\ s+\\frac{3}{2} & =2 \\\\ s & =2-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ s & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=\\frac{1}{2},\\,t=-\\frac{3}{4},$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{1}{2}b-\\frac{3}{4}c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $$\n\\displaystyle s\\cdot t=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{3}{4}\\right)=-\\frac{3}{8}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344944 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66b81663-6e80-51d7-a913-48b15173205e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343109} {:answer/id #uuid "8714c620-1893-528d-8182-61236ee13206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343405} {:answer/id #uuid "b53eaae6-d50b-5fbe-95be-daf4107639c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343824} {:answer/id #uuid "ec48cbca-b54e-529c-a456-f0f5a7c0d8b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344311} {:answer/id #uuid "ef0d8fa3-1d8c-594e-b99a-40e3f03c6dce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef0d8fa3-1d8c-594e-b99a-40e3f03c6dce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344340} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a27d35b-cc89-5818-8e8d-5ccf5c8819cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344757}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c8c4efc9-6266-5ebb-8bcb-7388b1494f8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-74605" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc,$ $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,3,6⟩$, $c=⟨1,-2,4⟩$, and  $u=⟨3,19,-10⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 19 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s+t &=3 \\\\ 3s-2t &=19 \\\\ 6s+4t &=-10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 19 \\\\ 6 & 4 & -10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 6 & 4 & -10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -28\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -28\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -32\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=-32,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of $s$ and $t$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc=u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $u$ does *not* lie on the plane $Π.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393417 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7eb8a46-2267-5072-8709-51251ce9e760" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393419} {:answer/id #uuid "4af5620d-a92f-5f04-b9d9-0982f3d2a131" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393420} {:answer/id #uuid "9db239d2-39ff-503c-9288-54070e1b2d71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393421} {:answer/id #uuid "145d4992-30fd-5d3a-9dbb-d5d2652afc6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393422} {:answer/id #uuid "fbde74ee-e78a-57a1-9751-28a91866994f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9db239d2-39ff-503c-9288-54070e1b2d71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393421} :answer-field/id #uuid "b06e84e5-8b15-54ef-8727-430594345689" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393418}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4018a53f-b299-52cf-a135-1013bf76ce32" :question/math-academy-id "q-74607" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,2,3⟩$, $c=⟨3,8,-7⟩$, and  $u=⟨9,22,-5⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 22 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s+3t &=9 \\\\ 2s+8t &=22 \\\\ 3s-7t &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 8 & 22 \\\\ 3 & -7 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -7 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -16 & -32\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+8{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s+3t &=9 \\\\ 2t &=4 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n2t=4\\,⟹\\,t=2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s+3t & =9 \\\\ s+3(2) & =9 \\\\ s & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=3,\\,t=2,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=3b+2c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=3\\cdot 2=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399461 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5469c2f4-10d4-551a-8387-1f41e195f9f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399463} {:answer/id #uuid "b5aaf75e-0319-5e2f-b6a1-406f9f457622" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399464} {:answer/id #uuid "6f0f386a-54e4-5bbd-999d-c5b1e894fea2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399465} {:answer/id #uuid "ea345608-0f4c-5f8a-9cea-a53c46ba68a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399466} {:answer/id #uuid "f370dd07-5630-5589-a9df-b8eef801b693" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f370dd07-5630-5589-a9df-b8eef801b693" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399467} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ded2025-f849-5e24-ae50-154d00e66f84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399462}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "da64bb93-914e-5229-bb6d-b7d97e6fa1bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-105248" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,-4,2⟩$, $c=⟨3,-10,2⟩$, and  $u=⟨-2,5,0⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s+3t &=-2 \\\\ -4s-10t &=5 \\\\ 2s+2t &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -10 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=-2,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of $s$ and $t$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc=u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $u$ does *not* lie on the plane $Π.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403766 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e98f85e7-255d-57c4-987f-635dd16edd05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403768} {:answer/id #uuid "22eae911-bfae-55d1-acf2-f7cf5e10e29a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403769} {:answer/id #uuid "a100b320-8f04-5bdd-8ea7-26f1cec017c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403770} {:answer/id #uuid "b4645d11-c80f-53cc-afba-0d87d9de8fa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403771} {:answer/id #uuid "d43a8623-8d3d-5185-9200-86c7e4e420c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403772}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d43a8623-8d3d-5185-9200-86c7e4e420c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403772} :answer-field/id #uuid "b97ac01d-f426-551c-8b2f-1c4b7bdf001e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403767}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "da2b75e4-b38a-5b5b-9891-19906308bd00" :question/math-academy-id "q-74600" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨-1,4,-5⟩$, $c=⟨3,-9,15⟩$, and  $u=⟨2,-2,11⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+3t &=2 \\\\ 4s-9t &=-2 \\\\ -5s+15t &=11\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -9 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 15 & 11\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -5 & 15 & 11\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=1,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of $s$ and $t$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc=u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $u$ does *not* lie on the plane $Π.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421528 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31aa51c7-7bbf-539a-8251-ca7e5420f8e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421502} {:answer/id #uuid "404186fe-c6bf-5419-b373-a5941944a534" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421505} {:answer/id #uuid "a5aeef05-ac8e-5ffc-b5cd-7dab5e605fc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421514} {:answer/id #uuid "cb1bdf10-0234-549d-b4c6-dcf3de7b6fdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421517} {:answer/id #uuid "ffbc367b-e607-5dad-b444-946e25112421" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421522}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31aa51c7-7bbf-539a-8251-ca7e5420f8e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421502} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe4e956c-1b1f-5312-af0b-3bb85188fdbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421527}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5b9c3557-0777-5517-a4eb-de326b8ca141" :question/math-academy-id "q-74609" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨-1,4,3⟩$, $c=⟨2,-6,-4⟩$, and  $u=⟨3,-7,-4⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+2t &=3 \\\\ 4s-6t &=-7 \\\\ 3s-4t &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -6 & -7 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+2t &=3 \\\\ 2t &=5 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n2t=5\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s+2t & =3 \\\\ -s+2\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right) & =3 \\\\ -s+5 & =3 \\\\ -s & =-2 \\\\ s & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=2,\\,t=\\frac{5}{2},$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=2b+\\frac{5}{2}c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=2\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421529 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a7a3f85-c316-5d92-9f90-b24c014d8770" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421500} {:answer/id #uuid "244d18d1-69c9-554a-801a-a1ee85e653f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421501} {:answer/id #uuid "49efebb4-5b44-54d8-a642-d7be1bed4e5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421507} {:answer/id #uuid "8c1e9e25-575f-5bba-bb57-6864dc973a15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421511} {:answer/id #uuid "f486e66a-d479-5a8a-b1e9-cfb2602b755d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421521}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a7a3f85-c316-5d92-9f90-b24c014d8770" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421500} :answer-field/id #uuid "2974b131-4f18-559b-891b-6b98e368f920" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421523}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9fca2b37-ca0d-5f9c-9cd0-c84b2660c1c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-34653" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2} &=10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=-5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-5.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+4(-5)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=20.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20{a}_{1}+(-5){a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 20\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+(-5)\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=20\\cdot (-5)=-100.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421530 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3730de20-b24e-5f5e-a26c-d563eb7c0ee1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421504} {:answer/id #uuid "43f2e466-d80e-55b3-9568-6896ede2a380" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421506} {:answer/id #uuid "7216d5b9-15dc-5173-80f7-9cff9ed9a669" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421508} {:answer/id #uuid "afae5c38-3c29-54c4-8923-744473be6095" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421515} {:answer/id #uuid "daa49e61-be48-5737-b796-4a269a8a98e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421520}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3730de20-b24e-5f5e-a26c-d563eb7c0ee1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421504} :answer-field/id #uuid "46a3e759-b5ee-59ce-9c0f-961ebc2fe588" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421525}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c75c18ab-94b6-560b-bd47-66c76f099710" :question/math-academy-id "q-105215" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2} &=3 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -6 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=1,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $b$ does *not* lie in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421531 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18da01e3-a753-5c12-b310-e49dbac1352a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421499} {:answer/id #uuid "8b330e4c-1039-5eb3-95e3-86ecad96d372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421510} {:answer/id #uuid "94545aa5-65f2-555f-8c83-9dc00de7552e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421512} {:answer/id #uuid "c506c166-ea56-5484-9ce8-55f2a4ef6b2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421516} {:answer/id #uuid "d5866e44-8aa4-58d9-b2ef-ad9461dd3c47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421519}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b330e4c-1039-5eb3-95e3-86ecad96d372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421510} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e5fe0f3-2bfd-5489-af0f-1a776954c9bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421526}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "cdba03e5-45ad-5856-b84f-f9bccefe0c86" :question/math-academy-id "q-105242" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 18 \\\\ 39\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 18 \\\\ 39\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2} &=-3 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+18{x}_{2} &=-6 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+39{x}_{2} &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 18 & -6 \\\\ 5 & 39 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 39 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & k+15\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & k+15\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+19\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+19.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+19\\,⇒\\,k=-19.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421532 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "118b15fa-3742-5277-8c58-23aa4caecb92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421498} {:answer/id #uuid "32eb1479-5bf7-5b7a-b94f-51a07f1faf34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421503} {:answer/id #uuid "8b2ff67d-5ecb-55cb-9c92-917e51071eb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421509} {:answer/id #uuid "961a42eb-d51a-527b-8228-58478af36cd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421513} {:answer/id #uuid "cce1ebbb-0068-52c9-a474-6ce0f6163af7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421518}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32eb1479-5bf7-5b7a-b94f-51a07f1faf34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421503} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d064b98-7b87-5c7b-a6e2-625fb2a9f2b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421524}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f6e087fb-be43-5d06-8b0f-af7c87178067" :question/math-academy-id "q-105241" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-8{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} &=5 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=-3 \\\\ -12{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2} &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -12 & -6 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -12 & -6 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -12 & -6 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-9\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-9.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-9\\,⇒\\,k=9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436138 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "711bff2a-6953-5410-bb47-66e0c9bf361e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436132} {:answer/id #uuid "94b9bad3-ee59-5063-a347-e17815281f18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436133} {:answer/id #uuid "a2f39043-eded-58ee-8538-d1b96c3a350b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436134} {:answer/id #uuid "a676903a-1471-5d07-b4fb-3436e54d4e03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436135} {:answer/id #uuid "caaab5ae-2e33-5881-8499-57baf2a35a93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436136}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "711bff2a-6953-5410-bb47-66e0c9bf36