:question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "996f5bdf-6de3-5168-a1d0-b97c26e1ea47" :question/problem "Find the value of $k$ such that $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\operatorname{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2\\}$, where\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_1=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad\\mathbf{a}_2=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the augmented matrix for $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2=\\mathbf{b}$ to determine when the system is consistent:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & k\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\operatorname{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2\\}$ exactly when $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2=\\mathbf{b}$ has a solution. Equating coordinates gives\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}- x_{1} - x_{2} &=3 \\\\ x_{1} + 2 x_{2} &=-3 \\\\ x_{1} + 2 x_{2} &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nForm the augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & k\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_1\\leftarrow (-1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & k\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_2\\leftarrow R_2-(1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & k\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_3\\leftarrow R_3-(1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & k + 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_3\\leftarrow R_3-(1)R_2$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k + 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe last row represents $0x_1+0x_2=k + 3$. Consistency therefore requires\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 &=k + 3 \\\\ k &=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot equations give $x_2=0$ and $x_1=-3$. These values also establish sufficiency:\n\n$$\n(-3)\\mathbf{a}_1+(0)\\mathbf{a}_2=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=-3$ is the only value for which the vector lies in the span."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713964 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "140ce550-6f64-57a7-96b1-bbcedd684765" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713946} {:answer/id #uuid "42d31477-2c22-55c4-b7d6-1e7217b62522" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713952} {:answer/id #uuid "74b8af6b-4af7-5064-bb89-04e67b5c3ffe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713958} {:answer/id #uuid "7e321976-0226-5cb5-83ec-c5751c4e21c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713959} {:answer/id #uuid "c6173ec0-bd57-55b5-baa3-437434d2914f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e321976-0226-5cb5-83ec-c5751c4e21c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713959} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc166dcd-c935-512f-b772-eb00261a0664" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713972}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a00b6d8d-2111-54c5-996f-dabc258db3ec" :question/problem "Find the value of $k$ such that $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\operatorname{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2\\}$, where\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_1=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad\\mathbf{a}_2=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ k \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the augmented matrix for $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2=\\mathbf{b}$ to determine when the system is consistent:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -2 & k \\\\ -1 & 2 & -10\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\operatorname{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2\\}$ exactly when $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2=\\mathbf{b}$ has a solution. Equating coordinates gives\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}- x_{1} + x_{2} &=-7 \\\\ x_{1} - 2 x_{2} &=k \\\\ - x_{1} + 2 x_{2} &=-10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nForm the augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -2 & k \\\\ -1 & 2 & -10\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nPlace the two known-coordinate equations first (a row permutation).\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -10 \\\\ 1 & -2 & k\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_1\\leftarrow (-1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -10 \\\\ 1 & -2 & k\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_2\\leftarrow R_2-(-1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & k\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_3\\leftarrow R_3-(1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & k - 7\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_3\\leftarrow R_3-(-1)R_2$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k - 10\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe last row represents $0x_1+0x_2=k - 10$. Consistency therefore requires\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 &=k - 10 \\\\ k &=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot equations give $x_2=-3$ and $x_1=4$. These values also establish sufficiency:\n\n$$\n(4)\\mathbf{a}_1+(-3)\\mathbf{a}_2=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=10$ is the only value for which the vector lies in the span."}]}
